{"diagnosis": "Recent results show no universal winner across families: latent_steps=3 helped retrieval (0.9961) but destroyed research (0.4121 vs 0.645 baseline), hidden=24 helped deduction (1.0), and state_partition=split helped research (0.7051 vs 0.645). The curation incumbent (relation+mean, TRM, direct feedback, 3 visits, hidden 32) sits at 0.7559 exact with adaptive early exit at ~1.26 visits and ece 0.046, i.e. it is already confidence-efficient but leaves accuracy on the table; the relation-weighted majority vote plus exact-twin flagging is a structured, certificate-friendly task, so latent refinement and certificate projection are the most plausible levers, not capacity.",
  "proposals": [
    {"config": {"latent_steps": 3}, "rationale": "The relation-weighted vote needs one extra fixed-point refinement of the latent workspace before the answer step; each latent step applies net(x+y+z) once, adding ~O(h^2) params (22019 -> ~24-26k) with zero FLOPs-per-visit change beyond one extra mixing pass. Expected gain ~+0.03 exact from better cluster-vote convergence, at the cost of ~10% more FLOPs.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.80, "falsification": "dev_exact <= 0.756 (incumbent) or >0.05 below prediction, mirroring the research-family collapse where latent_steps=3 hurt."},
    {"config": {"ldt_projection": true}, "rationale": "Duplicates (col 8) and majority-label disagreement are certificate-checkable facts; clamping certified scores removes the residual error the direct feedback cannot correct, and the repair round (round 6) showed projection is cheap (params 22019->~12-14k). Expected gain ~+0.03-0.04 on the exact-twin/inconsistent-vote subset; risk is overfitting to host certificate noise.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.79, "falsification": "dev_exact <= 0.756, or adaptive_exact falls below the incumbent's 0.7754, indicating certificates are not binding on this family."},
    {"config": {"hidden": 48}, "rationale": "The relation+mean aggregation with mixer_layers=2 must represent pairwise similarity-weighted votes over up to 16 candidates; h=32 under-parameterizes the mixer (weight-matrix params scale ~(48/32)^2=2.25x, total ~35-40k, still under 250k). Expected gain ~+0.02-0.03 on the cluster-vote boundary cases; risk is overfitting 300-step racing rung.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.79, "falsification": "dev_exact <= 0.756, or train/held-out gap grows beyond ~0.05, indicating capacity overfit rather than vote improvement."}
  ]}
